From b670cb4e0b06b95922f02937d637bfce3ae22a35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "D. Zack Garza" <dzackgarza@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:17:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 12/16] feat: deploy the checked Bliss repair into an unpacked
 copy

Consumers of the published image stay blocked on the Bliss ABI until a rebuilt
image is published, which is held. This adds the one implementation that lets an
existing unpacked copy carry the same checked repair without pretending the
image was fixed:

  docker/apply-bliss-repair.sh PATCH

It refuses a copy that is not the published revision or whose two touched files
have local changes, applies that commit's own patch, rebuilds only
src/sage/graphs/bliss.cpython-...so through /sage/builddir -- Ninja regenerates
the build files from the patched Meson and Meson installs the newer module --
runs the canonical-label (both backends, labelled and unlabelled) and
automorphism-order smoke tests, and records base revision, patch and module
digests in /opt/bliss-repair.json. A failing smoke restores the previous module
and the source files; a second run is a no-op.

Verified against the published unpacked copy: the deployment completed with
meson's install preserving 4516 unchanged files, the stamp records the base
revision b0cd7d8..., and the installed module now answers
Graph([[0,1]]).canonical_label(edge_labels=True) (previously a SIGSEGV), both
backends on a labelled graph, and automorphism groups of order 2, 8 and 120.
Nothing was published and no branch was created.
